     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, about twice the usual maximum. Labeling for immediate-release metformin generally caps the dose at about 2,550 mg/day (some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day), and 1700 mg isn't a standard tablet strength (500, 850, and 1000 mg are common). This looks like a possible dosing error, so please confirm the intended dose before I enter it.\n\nSome options:\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **500 mg PO TID with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO BID with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- Or, if 1700 mg TID is intentional, please tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note.\n\nAlso, is this a new start or a continuation? If it's a continuation, please check the home dose. Once you confirm, I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
